    <item>
      <title>The Sticky Quarter and the Ghost of the Future: George R.R. Martin on the World of Howard Waldrop</title>
      <link>https://motionographer.com/2026/01/30/the-sticky-quarter-and-the-ghost-of-the-future-george-r-r-martin-on-the-world-of-howard-waldrop/</link>
      <description>George R.R. Martin is stepping away from the Iron Throne to champion the 'weird-ass' imagination of his late friend, Howard Waldrop. Through a series of short films, including the dodo-bird mystery The Ugly Chickens, the indigenous post-apocalyptic Mary Margaret Road-Grader, and the Martian-invasion western Night of the Cooters, Martin is translating Waldrop’s idiosyncratic prose into a visual language that refuses to compromise.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://motionographer.com/2026/01/30/the-sticky-quarter-and-the-ghost-of-the-future-george-r-r-martin-on-the-world-of-howard-waldrop/</guid>
